n's suggested behavior.\n\n> In addition, I don't understand what the purpose of the config.debug function\n\nOne reason is that the core loop in pydicom (data_element_generator in filereader.py) is extremely optimized for speed - it checks the `debugging` flag set by config.debug, to avoid composing messages and doing function calls to logger when not needed.", 'repo_path': 'C:\\Users\\XF\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\evomas_workspace\\pydicom__pydicom-901'}
